  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), what HFR answers when the **owner** of a group MP replies through `message.php` with its `newdest` roster unchanged or edited. #336/#480 captured the roster as served (`R123c` owner, `R123e` member) but no POST from that form, so LOT-058 (#84) reads the roster and sends it back as served, and cannot offer to change it (never guess HFR behaviour, LESSONS 35-36).\n\n### Scope\n\nAll on the #336 fixture thread (`post=3207958`, owner user1, members user2 and user3) or a fresh group of the operator's own accounts. Each step is a **write**: the operator approves it first (AGENTS.md §0, §8 write log). For each POST keep the request body and the answer, then the pages named.\n\n1. **Unchanged roster**: owner's reply from the `R123c` form with `newdest` as served. Answer (is it W11's \"Votre réponse a été postée avec succès !\"?).\n2. **Add a member** (a fourth operator account): `newdest=\"user3, user2, user4\"`. Answer; then the thread page (owner, and the new member: redface2 E8 says HFR inserts a \"Modération\" system message), the owner's `message.php` form (new `newdest`), the new member's MP list row (`Interlocuteurs multiples` title).\n3. **Remove a member**: `newdest` without user3. Answer; the thread page; user3's MP list (row gone?) and user3's GET of the thread (the \"Ce message ne vous est pas destiné\" page of `RA5`?).\n4. **Empty roster** (the form says \"un destinataire au minimum !\"): `newdest=` empty. Answer (refusal sentence?).\n5. **Unknown pseudo** in `newdest`. Answer.\n6. Optional: a non-owner member's reply carrying a `newdest` field the form did not serve (is it ignored?).\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field (pseudos → `userN`, ids → `9000NN`, `--private` for subjects and bodies), MANIFEST rows, legacy oracles where a parser applies. Never hand-build these states in the cloud.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-058 (#84, group MP members: the roster write), and through it LOT-181 (#421, app: group members).\n\n### Depends on\n\nThe operator's approval for each write.\n\n### Source\n\nLOT-058 group-members PR (`docs/lots/LOT-058-mp-actions.md`, \"Pending capture\"); HFR-PROTOCOL §6c \"M2 write captures\".",
